<blockquote>
	<strong>Hiraeth (n.)</strong> — The sense of loss that comes from having been separated from one’s home; missing the feeling of being home, of having a place.
  </blockquote>
  
  <p>A Welsh word I've taken to describe my identity for the longest I can recall, when I was picking a name for a web magazine assignment for school. Ever since, it's become an integrated part of who I am.</p>
  
  <p>Part of exploring its meaning comes from looking for and embracing it in the themes of media, ranging from poetry to music, to films and paint.</p>
  
  <p>So comes this space as an archive of my fixations. Where I take apart tracks, movies, characters, and anything in between that intrigues me enough to dive deep into its meaning, till I surface again and share my analysis of it.</p>
  
  <p>I'm Lujain, and analysis is what we'll do.</p>
</Layout>
